			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, Chinese period-drama style, a medium-wide shot frames a young woman in a flowing jade-green hanfu ruqun walking slowly along the wet grey flagstones beside an ancient wooden temple, its upturned eaves and dark red pillars rising behind her. She holds a cream oil-paper umbrella above her head, its ribs casting a soft shadow across her face. Rain falls steadily through the frame, streaming off the eaves in thin silver threads and scattering into the puddles around her embroidered shoes. The camera holds a slow tracking shot, moving backward as she walks forward, her long skirt and silk sashes swaying gently with each step. [Shot 2] At 00:02.800, the shot cuts to a close-up of the umbrella's edge as rainwater gathers along the rim and drips away in a steady rhythm. She lowers the umbrella slightly, tilting her head to look up at the carved wooden brackets and the temple plaque above the doorway. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed as her eyes follow the rain falling past the eaves, and one loose strand of hair lifts in the damp breeze.\n\noverall_soundscape: Steady rain patters against the oil-paper umbrella and hisses across the wet flagstones. Water spills continuously from the temple eaves into the puddles below. Her silk skirt rustles softly with each step, and distant thunder rolls faintly over the courtyard.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: A slow guzheng melody with sparse, rippling notes, joined by a single bamboo flute phrase and low strings that swell gently under the rain before fading out.",
